  "name": "Aguinaldo venezolano (Venezuelan Christmas parranda)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Venezuelan aguinaldos are the Christmas songs carried from house to house by parrandas around Christmas, the religious aguinaldo telling of the Nativity and the secular parranda asking for food, drink and good cheer. The parranda plays cuatro, maracas, the furruco friction drum, a charrasca scraper and a small tambora drum, sometimes with guitar and mandolin, under a soloist answered by the group. The guayo card stands in for the charrasca and the membrane-drum card for the tambora.",
